WEBVTT

00:01.930 --> 00:03.810
<i>This is the Magic Realm.</i>

00:03.980 --> 00:07.690
<i>It is called the Magic Realm
because it is a world that has magic.</i>

00:08.270 --> 00:12.440
<i>Flying through the sky with a broom,
levitating heavy objects,</i>

00:12.440 --> 00:15.360
<i>creating something out of nothing...</i>

00:16.320 --> 00:19.120
<i>Everyone can use magic at their will,</i>

00:19.290 --> 00:22.710
<i>and in this world,
magic is a natural part of everyday life.</i>

00:23.370 --> 00:26.670
<i>Magic is believed to be a gift
bestowed by God,</i>

00:26.670 --> 00:31.050
<i>and mastery of magic determines
one's social status in this world.</i>

00:33.670 --> 00:38.140
<i>In a corner of this world,
where dragons flying about is ordinary...</i>

00:38.430 --> 00:41.390
<i>Within that deep, deep forest,</i>

00:41.930 --> 00:46.520
<i>there is one whose existence
defies the natural order.</i>

00:53.440 --> 00:56.240
Nothing like a cream puff
after pumping iron.

02:31.130 --> 02:34.210
<i>My name is Regro Burnedead.</i>

02:34.210 --> 02:36.510
<i>I'm a chic and elegant 75-year-old</i>

02:36.510 --> 02:42.050
<i>living with my son in a forest
far from other humans.</i>

02:45.310 --> 02:49.310
<i>I was quite reckless
in all sorts of ways in my youth,</i>

02:49.440 --> 02:53.310
<i>but when you get as old as I,
very little bothers you.</i>

02:54.770 --> 02:56.030
<i>And that’s because,</i>

02:56.570 --> 03:02.780
<i>through my experiences,
I have acquired ways to combat stress.</i>

03:02.870 --> 03:04.240
<i>How to combat stress...</i>

03:07.490 --> 03:09.830
Oh, Pops. I'm home.

03:11.960 --> 03:12.920
Why!?

03:12.920 --> 03:15.630
Why did you rip the door off
its hinges to come in, Mash!?

03:15.630 --> 03:17.880
I couldn't remember
if I was supposed to push or pull.

03:17.880 --> 03:20.090
How many years have you lived here!?

03:20.380 --> 03:21.800
So I just kind of forced—

03:21.800 --> 03:23.590
And you ended up breaking it!

03:24.890 --> 03:27.600
Sorry, Pops. I'll fix it.

03:28.180 --> 03:31.640
Oh, well... If you're repenting, then...

03:31.640 --> 03:34.610
<i>He's always so amenable
after each screwup.</i>

03:37.780 --> 03:39.860
Turn! Turn it! Turn it!
You need to turn it!

03:39.860 --> 03:42.610
- Weird. It won't fit back in.
- That's the wrong position!

03:43.110 --> 03:44.660
Huh? What'd you say?

03:44.660 --> 03:46.370
Quit with the pounding, would you!?

03:46.370 --> 03:47.540
Spit on the foundling?

03:47.540 --> 03:50.000
No!

03:52.460 --> 03:53.920
Sorry, Pops.

03:54.330 --> 03:55.460
I'll fix it.

03:55.460 --> 03:58.250
W-Well... Yeah, um...

03:59.960 --> 04:03.090
Mash, did you finish
today's training routine?

04:03.090 --> 04:04.220
Of course.

04:06.550 --> 04:07.850
Hey, Pops.

04:08.180 --> 04:09.720
I've been meaning to ask...

04:09.930 --> 04:11.770
Why are all of my workouts physical?

04:12.560 --> 04:13.850
Because you...

04:14.520 --> 04:17.310
<i>You're not like ordinary people.</i>

04:17.310 --> 04:21.650
<i>You can't use magic at all
because you're different.</i>

04:21.900 --> 04:23.610
<i>So the least I can do is...</i>

04:24.860 --> 04:27.530
Never mind. A story for another time.

04:27.620 --> 04:30.370
Anyway, I'm heading out for a bit.

04:30.660 --> 04:32.370
I'm trusting you to housesit.

04:32.370 --> 04:34.580
- Okay.
- Don't break the door.

04:35.040 --> 04:37.670
Don’t worry,
I learned how to fix it.

04:37.670 --> 04:40.000
Learn how to open and close
the door instead!

04:40.210 --> 04:41.550
Push in, or pull out...

04:41.550 --> 04:43.510
Pull out! Pull out to open the door!

04:44.260 --> 04:46.640
Anyways, I'm heading out.

04:47.850 --> 04:49.720
I've told you countless times before,

04:49.720 --> 04:53.390
but while I'm out, you must never
venture into the city.

04:53.640 --> 04:55.730
Yeah, I won't.

04:55.730 --> 04:59.400
Right. Mash, you’re such a good,
amenable son.

04:59.610 --> 05:01.360
Now, I'll be on my way.

05:01.360 --> 05:02.740
Be safe.

05:12.290 --> 05:13.660
<i>Sorry, Pops.</i>

05:14.210 --> 05:16.290
<i>But I can't ignore
the call of an empty stomach.</i>

05:26.680 --> 05:27.800
Magic.

05:28.680 --> 05:29.760
Magic.

05:30.550 --> 05:31.680
Magic.

05:33.600 --> 05:36.440
They're still just doing stuff
you can do with your hands.

05:43.320 --> 05:45.440
Seven limited cream puffs, please.

05:45.440 --> 05:46.450
Sure thing.

05:49.700 --> 05:52.990
Oops. I got too excited
and couldn't hold back.

05:53.870 --> 05:57.370
<i>But these don't usually bend
just by squeezing your hand.</i>

05:57.920 --> 05:59.880
Sorry. Let me fix them.

06:00.460 --> 06:01.710
Did you say, "fix"?

06:03.960 --> 06:05.550
This should work.

06:05.710 --> 06:07.840
<i>Huh? Hold on...</i>

06:09.050 --> 06:11.600
<i>Freaky? Huh? No, wait... Um...</i>

06:14.720 --> 06:16.230
Here. Thanks for waiting.

06:16.230 --> 06:17.810
Thank you very much.

06:21.310 --> 06:22.690
Hey, did you see it?

06:22.690 --> 06:24.360
I don't see it anywhere on his face.

06:24.360 --> 06:25.690
- No way.
- You're right. Nothing.

06:25.690 --> 06:27.110
Unbelievable.

06:27.740 --> 06:30.110
Sir, are you actually a...

06:31.450 --> 06:33.990
No, never mind.
Thanks for your patronage.

06:35.910 --> 06:38.620
<i>This year's "Divine Visionary"
has been determined.</i>

06:39.170 --> 06:44.210
<i>The one chosen as "Divine Visionary" is Rayne Ames,
a second-year at Easton Magic Academy,</i>

06:44.210 --> 06:47.130
<i>a prestigious school in the Magic Realm.</i>

06:47.460 --> 06:48.760
<i>This title is awarded</i>

06:48.760 --> 06:52.640
<i>to the student demonstrating the highest degree
of excellence over the school year.</i>

06:54.470 --> 06:59.350
Yeah, yeah.
Must feel good with all that talent.

07:00.270 --> 07:07.280
Then you have me here,
living a dull life in a dull place.

07:07.570 --> 07:12.780
P-Please forgive me.
I only stole a little something.

07:13.070 --> 07:15.530
Huh? Are you kidding me?

07:17.580 --> 07:20.920
You gave me more work
with your petty crime.

07:21.790 --> 07:27.130
I gotta make you regret it
so you’ll never trouble me again.

07:27.130 --> 07:29.550
S-Stop it! Please!

07:34.140 --> 07:36.560
What is it? I'm busy.

07:37.100 --> 07:41.140
What? There's an unmarked brat
in the city?

07:42.980 --> 07:45.820
Wonder what everyone
was all riled up about back there.

07:46.690 --> 07:50.440
<i>While I'm out, you must never
venture out into the city.</i>

07:51.320 --> 07:52.910
Sorry, Pops.

07:53.490 --> 07:55.570
But it was worth coming here.

07:56.120 --> 07:59.080
I got to eat Goblin Cream Puffs.

08:00.080 --> 08:02.830
Yummy, yummy, yum...

08:06.130 --> 08:07.090
Oh, sorry.

08:07.090 --> 08:08.750
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

08:08.920 --> 08:12.720
What do you think you’re doing?
I'm workin' over here!

08:12.720 --> 08:16.510
I'm a proud member of the magic police,
protecting ordinary folks like you!

08:17.720 --> 08:20.180
And do I get any thanks? No!

08:20.180 --> 08:22.940
The only thing I get is bottom-barrel pay!

08:22.940 --> 08:25.860
Wanna have me
take out my stress on ya?

08:28.690 --> 08:31.940
Would you like a cream puff?
I somehow feel sorry for you.

08:31.940 --> 08:33.530
He's pitying me!

08:33.530 --> 08:35.320
And it's half eaten!

08:36.490 --> 08:39.200
Why would you give me
a half-eaten cream puff?

08:39.200 --> 08:42.580
Ya aimin' for an indirect kiss or something?
Ya love me?

08:42.580 --> 08:44.670
Are ya pickin' a fight?

08:44.670 --> 08:46.920
That's basically pickin'
a fight with this country!

08:46.920 --> 08:50.960
And whatcha gonna do
about my uniform? Huh?

08:53.510 --> 08:54.720
<i>What?</i>

08:57.680 --> 09:00.970
I'm sorry. I will wash
and return these clothes to you.

09:01.020 --> 09:05.350
Now it ain't clothes!
Not as of this moment! Thanks to you!

09:05.690 --> 09:07.980
What exactly did ya do, huh?

09:07.980 --> 09:09.440
What's the matter, Terry?

09:09.690 --> 09:11.360
Brad, this kid...

09:11.730 --> 09:14.450
Don't make a riot over nothing.

09:14.700 --> 09:17.910
More like, why the hell are you naked?

09:20.120 --> 09:22.490
Well, that's because this kid...

09:23.370 --> 09:24.500
<i>Must be him.</i>

09:24.750 --> 09:28.250
<i>The unmarked brat from that report.</i>

09:28.580 --> 09:29.500
<i>Wait.</i>

09:29.790 --> 09:33.260
<i>Would anyone be eating cream puffs
in this kind of situation?</i>

09:34.170 --> 09:35.880
Hey, you over there.

09:37.840 --> 09:40.140
Please excuse my son!

09:47.980 --> 09:50.110
This will be a bit of a hassle,

09:50.110 --> 09:53.400
but this may be my chance
for a promotion.

09:56.990 --> 09:58.490
After them!

10:07.250 --> 10:08.750
You idiot!

10:08.960 --> 10:12.710
How may times have I told you?
Don't go to the city on your own!

10:12.710 --> 10:16.130
I'm really sorry. I'll never go again.

10:17.930 --> 10:21.800
<i>He's really broken up about it.
It's clear he regrets his actions.</i>

10:21.800 --> 10:23.890
<i>I can't stay mad at him.</i>

10:24.270 --> 10:28.020
Well, if that's the case, yeah.

10:28.230 --> 10:32.770
But as punishment, you'll repeat
this morning's training routine.

10:32.770 --> 10:36.860
Okay. And these cream puffs
are for you.

10:36.860 --> 10:38.860
Oh, thank you.

10:44.740 --> 10:45.580
Here.

10:45.580 --> 10:47.290
Thanks, Pops.

10:49.080 --> 10:50.880
<i>He's such a good boy.</i>

10:51.040 --> 10:53.750
<i>I thought a teenage son
would be really passionate,</i>

10:53.750 --> 10:56.260
<i>rife with arguments
and rebellious streaks,</i>

10:56.260 --> 10:59.130
<i>as you deepen your bonds
with each other.</i>

10:59.130 --> 11:03.050
<i>But he's so amenable,
though a bit informal.</i>

11:05.680 --> 11:08.930
<i>Well, I guess he's at an age
where he wants to get out.</i>

11:09.600 --> 11:15.190
<i>We've lived here in hiding until now,
away from the city in this forest, for his sake.</i>

11:15.690 --> 11:21.110
But now the magic police
have caught wind of him.

11:21.570 --> 11:23.820
I must act quickly.

11:29.160 --> 11:30.620
What is that?

11:42.840 --> 11:44.680
Hey, old geezer.

11:44.680 --> 11:47.100
Where's the brat I saw earlier?

11:48.140 --> 11:49.850
This is bad.

12:03.450 --> 12:06.530
Five minutes is all I need
when I put my mind to it.

12:06.780 --> 12:09.410
Time to head home and eat cream puffs.

12:10.500 --> 12:14.380
"Crea" a puff, a creamy puff.

12:14.380 --> 12:18.000
"Mp" a creamy, creamy puff.

12:18.000 --> 12:21.510
"uff" a puff, a creamy puff.

12:22.420 --> 12:25.180
Was I supposed to push or pull?

12:25.800 --> 12:27.220
Guess it doesn't matter.

12:27.220 --> 12:31.100
You knew and that's why
you hid that brat, right?

12:31.600 --> 12:36.400
You know why magic has flourished
since the dawn of recorded history?

12:37.020 --> 12:41.820
It's because we aggressively rid ourselves
of inferior blood unable to use magic.

12:43.280 --> 12:46.200
It's a necessary sacrifice
for the world to go round.

12:46.200 --> 12:51.580
Simply put, those who can't use magic
have no privileges.

12:52.450 --> 12:54.580
Privilege to live, that is.

12:55.080 --> 12:58.790
Or should I say,
they aren't supposed to live at all?

12:59.840 --> 13:02.340
Spill it. Where’s the brat?

13:02.800 --> 13:05.220
I-I have no idea
what you're talking about.

13:09.890 --> 13:14.390
Sheltering the unmarked
is a serious offense, old man.

13:14.770 --> 13:16.850
Hurry up and hand over the brat.

13:19.150 --> 13:20.360
I refuse!

13:23.070 --> 13:24.400
Fess up.

13:24.400 --> 13:29.870
If you play nice and give us the brat,
I'll have my bosses spare you.

13:30.280 --> 13:31.540
<i>I won’t.</i>

13:31.540 --> 13:34.660
<i>Never. I will never tell him.</i>

13:35.460 --> 13:38.130
Why can't you do something so simple!?

13:38.670 --> 13:39.630
I'm sorry.

13:39.880 --> 13:42.880
Your magic is weak.
You can't do anything properly!

13:42.880 --> 13:47.010
Our bloodline has no need
for failures like you!

13:47.840 --> 13:48.890
I'm sorry.

13:49.140 --> 13:52.010
Hey! You can't even do something
as simple as this?

13:52.350 --> 13:53.600
You're useless!

13:53.600 --> 13:55.020
I-I apologize.

13:55.020 --> 13:56.480
There are plenty of others
who can replace you!

13:56.480 --> 13:59.770
<i>I have always been a failure of a human.</i>

14:00.560 --> 14:03.780
<i>I kept failing
even after I became an adult.</i>

14:03.940 --> 14:05.570
<i>You messed up again!</i>

14:05.570 --> 14:06.900
<i>You're fired!</i>

14:06.900 --> 14:09.320
<i>How can you keep living like that?</i>

14:09.320 --> 14:12.120
<i>I'd already be dead
from embarrassment.</i>

14:19.210 --> 14:22.290
<i>Completely unwanted.</i>

14:22.290 --> 14:25.170
<i>I thought that's how my life would end.</i>

14:30.550 --> 14:33.600
<i>If that's the case, then I should just...</i>

14:42.940 --> 14:43.820
This baby...

14:44.440 --> 14:45.650
has no mark.

14:47.950 --> 14:50.870
You were abandoned
because you were unmarked.

14:52.700 --> 14:55.080
You're just like me.

15:00.580 --> 15:06.090
<i>In this moment, for the first time
in my life, I felt like someone needed me.</i>

15:07.420 --> 15:09.680
<i>I swore on that day...</i>

15:11.970 --> 15:18.600
<i>Even if we're not related by blood,
even if the entire world denied his existence,</i>

15:18.930 --> 15:22.310
<i>I would always be a father to that boy!</i>

15:22.560 --> 15:24.980
Tell us where he is already, old man.

15:25.230 --> 15:27.780
Run, Mash!

15:27.940 --> 15:29.200
You old geezer!

15:29.200 --> 15:32.740
Hey! This means
he's still close by! Find him!

15:32.740 --> 15:33.990
Yessir!

15:34.120 --> 15:35.580
Run for it, Mash!

15:35.740 --> 15:38.040
Damn you, old geezer!

15:39.500 --> 15:41.580
- L-Let go of me!
- Run! Run!

15:41.790 --> 15:43.580
Pipe it down, old geezer!

15:44.630 --> 15:46.500
<i>All that matters
is that you're safe! Please!</i>

15:46.500 --> 15:48.590
- Old man, hurry up and...
- Run away!

15:49.760 --> 15:52.890
<i>You are my one and only...</i>

15:53.010 --> 15:56.350
Run! Run away, Mash!

15:56.680 --> 15:59.310
That's enough, old man.

15:59.730 --> 16:01.600
I'll make you regret this.

16:26.290 --> 16:28.880
Hey you! You had some nerve
earlier today when...

16:31.010 --> 16:32.840
<i>My second shirt today...</i>

16:40.600 --> 16:41.850
Why...

16:41.850 --> 16:44.520
Why didn't you run, Mash?

16:45.020 --> 16:46.310
Because we're family.

16:47.060 --> 16:49.110
You're all I've got.

16:50.820 --> 16:53.450
Sorry for being selfish, Pops.

16:53.990 --> 16:55.490
But since I'm here...

16:57.200 --> 17:00.620
I might as well send you guys to hell.

17:03.250 --> 17:05.370
What a joke.

17:05.370 --> 17:09.460
You can't even use magic.
How are you going to take me down?

17:09.800 --> 17:14.970
<i>What an idiot. Brad used to be
on the Bureau of Magic's Security Force.</i>

17:14.970 --> 17:18.720
<i>Regular mages around here
don't hold a candle to him.</i>

17:18.800 --> 17:23.060
<i>And a magic-less chump
wants to take him on?</i>

17:23.060 --> 17:24.600
<i>He won't stand a chance!</i>

17:24.940 --> 17:27.190
It'll be over in three seconds.

17:30.360 --> 17:35.360
<i>That’s the spell that drove away a dragon
in his Bureau of Magic's Security Force days!</i>

17:35.360 --> 17:38.370
<i>I didn't think I would get to see it here!</i>

17:40.490 --> 17:42.080
Eat this.

17:42.700 --> 17:44.000
Nalcom Pas!

17:44.250 --> 17:46.080
Mash!

17:59.640 --> 18:00.890
Mash!

18:01.310 --> 18:03.020
<i>Huh? Did he...</i>

18:03.180 --> 18:06.350
<i>My Nalcom Pas... He just...</i>

18:06.890 --> 18:09.100
<i>He slapped it down? Like, “paff”?</i>

18:09.560 --> 18:12.480
<i>Can magic be paff'ed just like that?</i>

18:12.820 --> 18:15.820
<i>I drove a dragon away
with that spell, you know?</i>

18:15.820 --> 18:18.360
<i>What? There's no way.</i>

18:20.200 --> 18:22.450
Not bad, brat!

18:22.660 --> 18:24.910
But how about this?

18:25.290 --> 18:26.830
<i>That magical energy output!</i>

18:26.830 --> 18:29.000
<i>Is he trying to destroy
this entire area?</i>

18:29.120 --> 18:30.580
Hold on, Brad!

18:30.670 --> 18:32.170
You shouldn't do that!

18:32.170 --> 18:34.420
Nalcom Pas Diagorus!

18:43.470 --> 18:44.930
Damn it!

18:47.060 --> 18:48.310
<i>This brat...</i>

18:48.310 --> 18:50.310
<i>He's killing the momentum
with his knees!</i>

18:50.310 --> 18:51.980
<i>What a soft touch!</i>

18:52.480 --> 18:54.730
All right, then how about this?

18:56.320 --> 18:57.990
<i>And now he's juggling!</i>

19:00.070 --> 19:01.780
<i>Look at those dribbling moves!</i>

19:03.370 --> 19:05.870
<i>This brat is totally
making a fool of me.</i>

19:09.040 --> 19:11.330
Pops, I'm gonna borrow your wand.

19:11.500 --> 19:13.000
<i>What’s going on?</i>

19:13.250 --> 19:15.630
<i>He can use magic after all?</i>

19:17.090 --> 19:18.550
<i>Doesn't matter.</i>

19:19.510 --> 19:22.760
<i>Ordinary magic
won't even reach me anyway...</i>

19:43.570 --> 19:47.950
<i>I've never seen anyone
use a magic wand like that before.</i>

19:50.460 --> 19:53.330
Threaten my family again...

19:53.330 --> 19:54.340
and I'll kill you.

19:54.630 --> 19:58.130
<i>His training was only meant
to teach him self-defense.</i>

19:58.130 --> 20:00.090
<i>How is this physically possible?</i>

20:00.840 --> 20:03.090
<i>Either way, we're done for.</i>

20:03.090 --> 20:06.600
<i>Even if we fend them off
for now, in due time...</i>

20:08.890 --> 20:10.230
Interesting.

20:10.230 --> 20:12.440
Let's make a deal, Mushroom Head.

20:12.440 --> 20:16.900
Do what I ask, and I'll let you
and the old geezer slide.

20:16.980 --> 20:18.110
A deal?

20:18.400 --> 20:20.570
Once a year in this country,

20:20.570 --> 20:24.240
one exceptional student
is revered as one of God's chosen.

20:24.240 --> 20:26.620
It's called the "Divine Visionary."

20:27.200 --> 20:31.000
Enroll in a magic school
and be chosen as one.

20:31.290 --> 20:36.000
Simply put, if you're selected,
it means God has accepted you.

20:36.290 --> 20:39.170
Which means, society will accept you.

20:39.170 --> 20:43.130
I just want the fortune and prestige
that comes with it.

20:43.300 --> 20:44.970
I'll back you up, of course.

20:44.970 --> 20:46.760
Don't listen to him, Mash!

20:46.800 --> 20:49.850
Those are the words of someone
who was an enemy until moments ago!

20:50.680 --> 20:53.100
It's up to you
if you want to be skeptical or not.

20:53.100 --> 20:56.520
But if you refuse, we’ll hunt you down
for the rest of your life.

20:58.150 --> 21:01.490
If I'm after you,
the whole country will be, too.

21:01.610 --> 21:05.910
You'll be okay because you're tough.
But what about the old man?

21:06.490 --> 21:11.410
A life where you can never feel at ease,
and unable to set foot in a city.

21:11.540 --> 21:13.960
Well, the choice is yours.

21:14.170 --> 21:16.790
Spend the rest of your life
being hunted down,

21:16.790 --> 21:20.250
or brace yourself to die
and try turning the tables?

21:24.010 --> 21:27.340
- You got a deal.
- Are you sane? It's a magic school!

21:27.720 --> 21:31.640
I'll be fine, Pops. My motivation
is stronger than anyone else.

21:31.640 --> 21:34.230
This isn't about motivation!

21:34.310 --> 21:35.440
Besides...

21:35.440 --> 21:38.110
I want us to be able
to live in peace again.

21:38.360 --> 21:40.360
<i>You're such a good boy.</i>

21:40.360 --> 21:41.980
<i>My son!</i>

21:43.940 --> 21:45.950
Living in peace with Pops.

21:47.410 --> 21:50.330
If it's a world that won't allow
something as natural as that...

21:57.790 --> 21:59.920
Then I've got no choice but to crush it.

22:01.210 --> 22:02.550
With my fist.
